    "note": "240 W across the 8 PoE+ ports - nearly twice the 125 W of the M4250-10G2F-PoE+ on the same eight-port copper block, because this model carries a 10G uplink pair and was given the larger supply."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. Rack model with the ports at the rear and a black display panel at the front; reversed mounting with the ports at the front is supported. Same 8 PoE+ / 2 copper / 2 SFP+ census as the M4250-10G2XF-PoE++, which swaps the 802.3at PSEs for Ultra90 802.3bt and a 720 W budget. Console: RJ45 RS232 plus USB-C, both at the rear. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
